1
00:00:15,829 --> 00:00:19,668
<i>SAWYER FARM
ESTABLISHED 1845

2
00:00:21,294 --> 00:00:30,348
<i># Happy birthday to you...

3
00:00:30,472 --> 00:00:35,313
<i># Happy birthday, dear Jed...

4
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:40,234
<i># Happy birthday to you...

5
00:00:40,359 --> 00:00:42,071
All right, now make a wish.

6
00:00:42,106 --> 00:00:43,073
Blow them out.

7
00:00:47,868 --> 00:00:50,121
Yes! Very good!

8
00:00:50,162 --> 00:00:52,332
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

9
00:00:52,373 --> 00:00:53,584
Very good!

10
00:00:53,708 --> 00:00:55,002
All right...

11
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,886
Drayton, where are your manners?

12
00:01:00,969 --> 00:01:03,138
Give the first slice to the thief.

13
00:01:17,905 --> 00:01:19,386
I didn't steal your damn pigs...

14
00:01:19,421 --> 00:01:20,868
Are you calling my son a liar?

15
00:01:20,993 --> 00:01:23,246
He saw your filthy hands stealing our property...

16
00:01:27,832 --> 00:01:30,629
Why would I go anywhere near your filthy pigs?

17
00:01:30,753 --> 00:01:32,215
Or your filthy family!

18
00:01:32,298 --> 00:01:35,385
I swear, everybody will know what kind of...

19
00:01:35,426 --> 00:01:37,304
...offspring you're raising here, Verna!

20
00:01:37,386 --> 00:01:39,223
Shut him up! I've had enough!

21
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,733
Listen to me, no farmhand is going to...

22
00:01:42,768 --> 00:01:44,564
...ruin my son's special night.

23
00:01:47,817 --> 00:01:49,194
Ready for your present?

24
00:01:52,489 --> 00:01:54,492
You know you're my special boy.

25
00:01:55,075 --> 00:01:57,162
Come on, Jed. There you go...

26
00:01:59,999 --> 00:02:02,252
- Jed.
- Yes, that's it, Jed.

27
00:02:04,755 --> 00:02:05,799
Now remember,

28
00:02:06,007 --> 00:02:09,136
bad people like him try to destroy our family.

29
00:02:09,761 --> 00:02:11,556
But we won't let that happen, will we?

30
00:02:11,722 --> 00:02:13,098
Go on, pick it up...

31
00:02:13,891 --> 00:02:15,393
Jed, pick it up...

32
00:02:15,934 --> 00:02:16,770
Jed!

33
00:02:16,894 --> 00:02:20,523
Jed...

34
00:02:20,564 --> 00:02:22,110
Pick it up, Jed!

35
00:02:22,151 --> 00:02:25,447
Jed!

36
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,241
Come on, you know what you have to do...

37
00:02:28,658 --> 00:02:30,371
That's it, Jed!

38
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:33,791
Come on, Jed...

39
00:02:34,499 --> 00:02:37,337
Jed!

40
00:02:37,419 --> 00:02:38,880
No!

41
00:02:38,921 --> 00:02:40,174
There you go.

42
00:02:40,590 --> 00:02:41,842
Go on, son!

43
00:02:41,877 --> 00:02:43,178
No!

44
00:02:49,892 --> 00:02:51,604
No!

45
00:02:57,194 --> 00:02:59,281
No!

46
00:02:59,447 --> 00:03:01,283
No, please!

47
00:03:01,408 --> 00:03:04,203
No!

48
00:03:04,244 --> 00:03:06,873
Do it, do it, do it!

49
00:03:06,914 --> 00:03:08,875
No!

50
00:03:08,916 --> 00:03:10,627
Go on, Jed, do it...

51
00:03:11,586 --> 00:03:12,630
Do it!

52
00:03:13,214 --> 00:03:15,426
- Jed.
- Do it!

53
00:03:21,723 --> 00:03:22,851
Mom!

54
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:24,894
Mom, no!

55
00:03:26,646 --> 00:03:29,985
No!

56
00:03:39,871 --> 00:03:40,706
Hey.

57
00:03:40,997 --> 00:03:42,584
You let us down, Jed.

58
00:03:45,336 --> 00:03:48,423
It's all right. Family will always be here for
you.

59
00:03:48,589 --> 00:03:49,924
Remember that.

60
00:03:50,675 --> 00:03:51,718
All right.

61
00:04:09,406 --> 00:04:14,497
<i>TEXAS, 1955

62
00:04:17,498 --> 00:04:18,919
Are you trying to get us killed?

63
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:19,836
Do you want me to stop?

64
00:04:19,878 --> 00:04:21,129
No, I didn't say that.

65
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:29,516
Watch out!

66
00:04:34,229 --> 00:04:36,025
What the hell was that thing?

67
00:04:37,316 --> 00:04:38,528
Hey, Betty.

68
00:04:45,743 --> 00:04:46,995
What is it?

69
00:04:48,287 --> 00:04:49,415
I don't know.

70
00:04:52,668 --> 00:04:54,130
Then let's go.

71
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:04,392
What?

72
00:05:12,776 --> 00:05:14,112
He's just a kid!

73
00:05:16,156 --> 00:05:17,450
Let's go!

74
00:05:17,824 --> 00:05:19,243
We'll be late.

75
00:05:21,370 --> 00:05:22,872
Hello.

76
00:05:27,128 --> 00:05:28,422
Are you okay?

77
00:05:34,553 --> 00:05:36,598
You shouldn't play in the road.

78
00:05:36,764 --> 00:05:38,725
Help me, please...

79
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,861
Hey, Betty, where are you going? I didn't hit him!

80
00:05:47,277 --> 00:05:48,905
- Something's wrong.
- Betty!

81
00:05:48,945 --> 00:05:50,365
He needs help.

82
00:05:50,907 --> 00:05:52,325
Jesus Christ!

83
00:05:56,747 --> 00:05:58,709
Hey, buddy, can you hear me?

84
00:06:00,711 --> 00:06:02,254
Let me help you!

85
00:06:06,132 --> 00:06:07,301
Hello?

86
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:16,522
It's okay. You can come out.

87
00:06:17,979 --> 00:06:19,108
Betty.

88
00:06:22,903 --> 00:06:24,614
Betty, where did you go?

89
00:07:22,894 --> 00:07:24,189
Hello?

90
00:07:29,361 --> 00:07:32,907
Come on... I won't hurt you.

91
00:07:35,450 --> 00:07:36,953
I just want to help...

92
00:07:44,003 --> 00:07:45,172
Okay?

93
00:07:56,061 --> 00:08:00,358
<i>BASED ON CHARACTERS CREATED BY

94
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:03,404
<i>KIM HENKEL AND TOBE HOOPER

95
00:08:05,697 --> 00:08:07,741
You did good, Jed!

96
00:08:08,533 --> 00:08:11,579
It's like... I can still feel you in there
after all.

97
00:08:42,907 --> 00:08:46,496
Well, let him learn a little more.

98
00:08:49,957 --> 00:08:51,502
Oh, my God!

99
00:09:01,138 --> 00:09:02,057
Show him!

100
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,657
- Where is she?
- Calm down, Hal.

101
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:18,744
Let me through, damn it!

102
00:09:18,785 --> 00:09:20,330
Let me go! Let me go, damn it!

103
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:21,955
- We know what happened.
- Calm down, Hal.

104
00:09:22,121 --> 00:09:23,750
Is that my little girl in there?

105
00:09:25,251 --> 00:09:28,130
Is she in there? Is my little girl in there?

106
00:09:28,464 --> 00:09:29,841
Answer me, damn it!

107
00:09:30,174 --> 00:09:31,551
We've got one of them.

108
00:09:35,930 --> 00:09:37,309
Oh, boy!

109
00:09:41,479 --> 00:09:42,857
I couldn't get to her in time!

110
00:09:43,065 --> 00:09:45,110
I'm so sorry, sir. I swear to God.

111
00:09:47,611 --> 00:09:49,322
Drayton Sawyer...

112
00:09:51,824 --> 00:09:53,703
It's time to go to Gorman Reformatory.

113
00:09:53,744 --> 00:09:57,083
No... You're all grown up now.

114
00:09:59,334 --> 00:10:01,338
That means the gas chamber for you.

115
00:10:05,008 --> 00:10:06,262
Why?

116
00:10:06,594 --> 00:10:08,431
Are you going to arrest me for finding a dead
body?

117
00:10:08,638 --> 00:10:10,100
Last I checked, that wasn't a crime.

118
00:10:10,149 --> 00:10:12,903
How about a bullet hole in your damn skull?

119
00:10:13,569 --> 00:10:14,869
- Put it away, Hal.
- Come on.

120
00:10:14,904 --> 00:10:16,782
He's right. We've got nothing on him...

121
00:10:17,156 --> 00:10:18,365
Calm down, Hal.

122
00:10:18,573 --> 00:10:19,325
Keep your head clear.

123
00:10:19,365 --> 00:10:21,869
- Hal, it's not worth it.
- Come on, Hal, lower the gun.

124
00:10:21,993 --> 00:10:23,329
Damn trash.

125
00:10:34,505 --> 00:10:36,466
Let those boys go right this instant!

126
00:10:36,757 --> 00:10:38,426
Don't count on it, Verna!

127
00:10:39,176 --> 00:10:40,637
Do you think they did anything wrong?

128
00:10:40,677 --> 00:10:41,763
No, I don't!

129
00:10:41,845 --> 00:10:43,681
You bastard, let them out of the car!

130
00:10:44,181 --> 00:10:46,976
No! They're going to stay there and rot!

131
00:10:48,059 --> 00:10:49,144
On what charges?

132
00:10:49,435 --> 00:10:50,729
They're not under arrest.

133
00:10:50,770 --> 00:10:53,065
They're in protective custody... from you.

134
00:10:53,106 --> 00:10:54,358
What are you talking about?

135
00:10:55,358 --> 00:10:57,903
I can't count how many crime scenes I've been
to...

136
00:10:57,944 --> 00:11:00,281
...where there's always a Sawyer involved.

137
00:11:00,823 --> 00:11:02,616
Those boys aren't safe with you...

138
00:11:02,698 --> 00:11:03,826
Bullshit.

139
00:11:04,742 --> 00:11:07,080
Get a warrant for the Sawyer house.

140
00:11:07,412 --> 00:11:09,457
Name every one of them. I want them all.

141
00:11:09,623 --> 00:11:10,625
- Did you hear me?
- You can't do that.

142
00:11:10,707 --> 00:11:11,584
You can't do that!

143
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:13,378
Well, by the time we get there, I'll have a
warrant saying I can...

144
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:14,921
...do just that.

145
00:11:15,587 --> 00:11:17,714
It's called "children at risk."

146
00:11:19,132 --> 00:11:21,093
You took one of mine...

147
00:11:21,843 --> 00:11:24,263
...so I'll take every one of yours, Verna.

148
00:11:30,435 --> 00:11:31,811
Every last one of them...

149
00:11:33,813 --> 00:11:35,816
<i>10 YEARS LATER

150
00:11:36,274 --> 00:11:39,945
<i>In 1935, the state of Texas established a...

151
00:11:39,986 --> 00:11:42,489
<i>...program to care for children at risk.

152
00:11:42,655 --> 00:11:45,993
In its first year, nearly 52 children were
removed from homes...

153
00:11:46,074 --> 00:11:48,911
...known to be involved in criminal activity.

154
00:11:49,244 --> 00:11:52,124
<i>Many of these children were given new names...

155
00:11:52,165 --> 00:11:53,959
<i>...and placed in foster homes.

156
00:11:54,083 --> 00:11:57,671
<i>Others, products of degenerate parenting...

157
00:11:57,712 --> 00:12:00,549
<i>...ended up here at Gorman Reformatory.

158
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:01,965
<i>GORMAN HOUSE JUVENILE REFORMATORY

159
00:12:02,006 --> 00:12:06,136
We take care of their physical and
psychological needs.

160
00:12:06,594 --> 00:12:07,847
Yes, sir.

161
00:12:07,971 --> 00:12:10,767
I've wanted to come here for a long time.

162
00:12:11,057 --> 00:12:12,393
I think I can help them.

163
00:12:12,559 --> 00:12:13,603
Elizabeth.

164
00:12:13,643 --> 00:12:15,271
Please, sir, Lizzy. Lizzy is fine.

165
00:12:15,312 --> 00:12:16,813
Elizabeth.

166
00:12:17,772 --> 00:12:20,025
Most of these children will end up...

167
00:12:20,065 --> 00:12:22,277
...in prisons or mental institutions.

168
00:12:23,319 --> 00:12:26,783
Keeping them here makes everyone safer.

169
00:12:27,574 --> 00:12:28,826
Keep your guard up.

170
00:13:13,494 --> 00:13:14,871
Well... hello...

171
00:13:15,704 --> 00:13:17,165
My name is Lizzy.

172
00:13:17,248 --> 00:13:20,127
I'm new here, and I'd like to get to know you.

173
00:13:24,672 --> 00:13:26,007
That's Bud.

174
00:13:27,633 --> 00:13:30,009
He doesn't say much for such a big guy.

175
00:13:35,432 --> 00:13:36,434
You're in my seat.

176
00:13:36,975 --> 00:13:38,144
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:39,018 --> 00:13:41,021
- Very nice.
- I'm...

178
00:13:41,062 --> 00:13:43,107
Lizzy... Yeah, I heard. I heard.

179
00:13:44,106 --> 00:13:46,276
Shit, sorry. I'm Jackson.

180
00:13:47,067 --> 00:13:50,030
Jackson and... Bud...

181
00:13:50,822 --> 00:13:53,284
And what medication are you taking, Jackson?

182
00:13:53,450 --> 00:13:54,660
Medication?

183
00:13:55,869 --> 00:13:57,830
They already gave it to us when they brought
us in, right?

184
00:13:58,829 --> 00:14:01,749
We figured you'd know more about that than we
do, Lizzy...

185
00:14:02,749 --> 00:14:05,171
You're not going to give me any trouble, are you?

186
00:14:05,670 --> 00:14:07,131
No, not me, Lizzy.

187
00:14:08,465 --> 00:14:09,764
Is there a reason you keep...

188
00:14:09,799 --> 00:14:11,343
...saying my name like that?

189
00:14:11,926 --> 00:14:16,180
No... I just like to know who's in charge,
that's all.

190
00:14:19,265 --> 00:14:20,935
Fuck you, asshole!

191
00:14:20,976 --> 00:14:21,895
I'll kick your ass.

192
00:14:21,935 --> 00:14:23,688
I'll fuck up your head!

193
00:14:23,812 --> 00:14:24,898
Let him go!

194
00:14:24,938 --> 00:14:26,483
Mind your own business!

195
00:14:26,607 --> 00:14:27,990
It is my business.

196
00:14:28,025 --> 00:14:29,443
What's the problem?

197
00:14:29,942 --> 00:14:32,362
He said something I didn't like.

198
00:14:32,653 --> 00:14:36,158
About what a girl in a nurse's uniform would
taste like.

199
00:14:37,033 --> 00:14:38,620
Hey, hey, let go of me!

200
00:14:38,911 --> 00:14:40,288
Let go!

201
00:14:41,121 --> 00:14:42,707
Fuck you, Frankenstein!

202
00:14:42,748 --> 00:14:44,374
That's enough. Stop it.

203
00:14:44,749 --> 00:14:47,170
- Ike, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

204
00:14:50,214 --> 00:14:51,424
Everything's fine.

205
00:15:52,399 --> 00:15:54,026
What are you doing?

206
00:15:58,988 --> 00:16:00,282
Come here.

207
00:16:03,618 --> 00:16:05,121
What's the problem?

208
00:16:05,162 --> 00:16:06,998
It's just a stupid mouse.

209
00:16:09,875 --> 00:16:11,169
Got a light?

210
00:16:11,251 --> 00:16:13,086
You know smoking isn't allowed in here...

211
00:16:15,379 --> 00:16:17,758
I have special permission.

212
00:16:18,550 --> 00:16:19,802
True story.

213
00:16:19,843 --> 00:16:21,763
Ask Dr. Lang.

214
00:16:21,970 --> 00:16:22,805
I will.

215
00:16:22,846 --> 00:16:24,807
He'll tell you it helps me.

216
00:16:25,891 --> 00:16:28,517
With my anxiety.

217
00:16:31,770 --> 00:16:33,314
The truth is...

218
00:16:34,355 --> 00:16:36,485
...it's because I'm his favorite.

219
00:16:36,859 --> 00:16:38,321
He told me so.

220
00:16:38,528 --> 00:16:41,198
- You've earned yourself a warning.
- Why?

221
00:16:41,238 --> 00:16:42,783
I was just taking a bath.

222
00:16:42,823 --> 00:16:44,159
Get out.

223
00:16:47,578 --> 00:16:48,872
Bitch.

224
00:16:50,706 --> 00:16:52,460
Is everything all right?

225
00:16:53,168 --> 00:16:55,379
Yes, Doctor, I'm fine.

226
00:16:55,961 --> 00:17:00,842
I'll handle Isaac and Bud.

227
00:17:00,925 --> 00:17:02,677
No. Bud didn't do anything.

228
00:17:02,718 --> 00:17:05,117
I look forward to our session tomorrow, Jackson.

229
00:17:05,152 --> 00:17:07,516
I'm sorry, but he's actually right.

230
00:17:07,556 --> 00:17:08,851
Bud didn't do anything.

231
00:17:08,892 --> 00:17:11,018
He was fighting...

232
00:17:11,643 --> 00:17:13,312
Well, he was protecting me...

233
00:17:13,394 --> 00:17:14,647
Remind me to tell you later what...

234
00:17:14,687 --> 00:17:16,273
...he did to his last foster family.

235
00:17:16,356 --> 00:17:18,025
Well, they took his dog away.

236
00:17:18,566 --> 00:17:21,862
Yes... that's a perfectly good reason...

237
00:17:21,903 --> 00:17:24,532
...to put someone in a coma.

238
00:17:24,907 --> 00:17:26,408
Well, I'm just saying.

239
00:17:48,846 --> 00:17:49,764
<i>DIAGNOSIS: BIPOLAR DISORDER

240
00:17:49,805 --> 00:17:53,726
<i>Upon admission, this 16-year-old boy,
Horton, Bud, was depressed, agitated and
fearful.

241
00:17:53,851 --> 00:17:56,894
<i>Overall, his behavior was aggressive,
unusually energetic and withdrawn.

242
00:18:00,106 --> 00:18:01,942
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

243
00:18:02,692 --> 00:18:04,027
You didn't.

244
00:18:04,777 --> 00:18:06,363
Thank you for helping Bud.

245
00:18:07,447 --> 00:18:11,075
I know you don't even know him, so that was nice.

246
00:18:11,825 --> 00:18:14,745
Well, I'm here to help you all. So...

247
00:18:16,497 --> 00:18:18,792
You're the first pretty nurse we've had around
here.

248
00:18:21,669 --> 00:18:23,255
So I thought you should know...

249
00:18:24,756 --> 00:18:25,924
Know what?

250
00:18:26,257 --> 00:18:28,887
What goes on in the relaxation room...

251
00:18:29,803 --> 00:18:31,682
The kids around here call it...

252
00:18:31,848 --> 00:18:34,101
...Dr. Lang's chamber of horrors.

253
00:18:34,517 --> 00:18:36,103
Piece of shit.

254
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:37,938
Why is that?

255
00:18:38,313 --> 00:18:40,814
Go there at night and find out for yourself...

256
00:18:42,356 --> 00:18:44,860
Hey, you might even do something about it.

257
00:18:46,235 --> 00:18:47,321
You know.

258
00:18:48,489 --> 00:18:49,616
Jackson...

259
00:18:51,909 --> 00:18:54,077
You'll get out of here one day.

260
00:18:54,368 --> 00:18:56,997
And just because you can't trust certain people...

261
00:18:58,498 --> 00:19:00,626
...doesn't mean you shouldn't trust others.

262
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:03,337
Well, I'll think about it.

263
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,219
<i>DR. LANG

264
00:19:14,806 --> 00:19:16,308
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

265
00:19:16,390 --> 00:19:19,061
Barry Farnsworth, we had an appointment an
hour ago.

266
00:19:19,143 --> 00:19:20,562
Did we?

267
00:19:22,856 --> 00:19:24,398
Mrs. Sawyer.

268
00:19:24,564 --> 00:19:26,734
It's Mrs. Carson now.

269
00:19:32,823 --> 00:19:34,408
I want to see Jed.

270
00:19:34,741 --> 00:19:36,828
We've been through this before.

271
00:19:37,327 --> 00:19:38,704
Year after year...

272
00:19:38,745 --> 00:19:40,081
He's my son.

273
00:19:40,497 --> 00:19:42,125
And I can afford a lawyer now.

274
